# Authorization identity source

## Plugin semantics

Authorization needs an identity object/actor. That identity may come from `cakephp/authentication`, custom middleware, or other project mechanisms.

## Required behavior

- Inspect Composer and app bootstrap before recommending Authentication APIs.
- If Authentication is absent, use the project’s existing identity approach.
- If Authentication is present (or both packs enabled), follow the integration guidance when available.

## Anti-patterns

- Requiring `cakephp/authentication` solely because Authorization is installed
- Hard-coding a fake admin identity in policies for convenience
